# 01 Base Measures

Additive facts and the two habits everything else depends on: DIVIDE for safe ratios, and capacity read from the dimension rather than the fact.

Read in file order — each measure builds on the ones before it.

- **`01_Marketing_Spend.dax`** — Sum of vendor spend at the current grain.
- **`02_Impressions.dax`** — Awareness volume by vendor.
- **`03_Clicks.dax`** — Click volume by vendor.
- **`04_Leads_Funnel.dax`** — Leads sourced through the marketing funnel.
- **`05_New_Leases_Funnel.dax`** — Leases carrying a marketing journey.
- **`06_Leads_Actual.dax`** — Leads the property recorded.
- **`07_Visits_Actual.dax`** — Property visits recorded.
- **`08_New_Leases_Actual.dax`** — All leases signed.
- **`09_Occupied_Units.dax`** — Units occupied at the snapshot.
- **`10_Vacant_Units.dax`** — Units vacant at the snapshot.
- **`11_Available_Units.dax`** — Units available to lease.
- **`12_Total_Units.dax`** — Physical capacity.
- **`13_Occupancy_Rate.dax`** — Occupied over occupied plus vacant.
- **`14_Vacancy_Rate.dax`** — The inverse view.
